  "Carnegie gave $20,000 in 1902; Lewis Merriman gave the site of the William M. Chesney house, books went in late in 1904, and it was dedicated on February 17, 1905 (Wikipedia says it was designed in 1905). Richards, McCarty and Bulford of Columbus drew it: a storey and a half of brick on a raised base, with a white marble entry and reading rooms with fireplaces. The library left on March 17, 1968; the Hardin County Historical Society leased it until 1983, it was auctioned in 1995 and was a hair salon before the dental office now in it. On the National Register since 1983.",
