  "Carnegie gave $13,600 in 1903 and the library was finished in 1904 to a design by Robert E. Schmidt of Chicago; in this railroad town the Nickel Plate road helped support it, and a townsman gave $5,000 for books. A 9,000-square-foot addition came in 1987.",
